    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "In Legacy, choosing to be on the draw gives up significant tempo advantage. While the hand lacks colored mana sources (only Wasteland), the extra draw doesn't compensate for losing the play. The hand likely needs a mulligan regardless of play/draw choice, and going first with a mulliganed hand is generally better than going second with this hand.",
      "action_taken": "Chose GPT5n Coach as starting player, putting themselves on the draw",
      "better_line": "Choose to be on the play (select Gem3P Spike as starting player). The tempo advantage of going first in Legacy is substantial, especially with Wasteland and Force of Will in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 1,
      "player": "Gem3P Spike",
      "decision_index": 0,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Tundra exposes it to opposing Wasteland on turn 1. In Legacy, leading with a fetchland is generally preferred to protect dual lands. Additionally, cracking Misty Rainforest puts a land in the graveyard for Life from the Loam synergy already in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Played Tundra as the turn 1 land",
      "better_line": "Play Misty Rainforest, crack it to fetch Tundra (or another blue source), then cast Ponder. This protects against opponent's Wasteland, puts a land in the graveyard for Life from the Loam, and still casts the turn 1 cantrip. The fetchland can't be saved for Brainstorm shuffle if you need blue mana now anyway, though saving it for Brainstorm is a counterargument.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "Gem3P Spike",
      "decision_index": 6,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "When ordering cards for Ponder, put Flooded Strand at the bottom of the three cards instead of Leyline Binding. Flooded Strand is a much more useful card right now (provides a land drop and mana fixing), while Leyline Binding costs effectively 4 mana with current domain and is uncastable for several turns.",
      "action_taken": "Put Flooded Strand at the bottom of the Ponder ordering (first chosen = bottommost)",
      "better_line": "Put Leyline Binding at the bottom (choose it first), keeping Flooded Strand closer to the top to draw sooner. Ideal order top-to-bottom: Flooded Strand, Ponder, Leyline Binding.",
